      ],
      "source": "https://discoveringmontana.com/towns/helena-flats/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Helena Flats sits beside the Flathead River, which shapes local agriculture and provides a scenic backdrop without dominating the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/helena_flats_montana",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s flat terrain, once dominated by 80‑ and 160‑acre farms, shifted to residential development in the 1950s thanks to its proximity to Kalispell.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/helena_flats_montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Helena Flats experiences a cold, humid continental climate (Dfb), with distinct seasons and milder temperatures than more exposed Montana areas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
